otropic effects of peroxisome proliferators</article-title><source><italic>Molecular and Cellular Biology</italic></source><year>1995</year><volume>15</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>3012</fpage><lpage>3022</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7539101</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B70"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tureyen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapadia</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowen</surname><given-names>KK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor-<italic>&#x003b3;</italic> agonists induce neuroprotection following transient focal ischemia in normotensive, normoglycemic as well as hypertensive and type-2 diabetic rodents</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Neurochemistry</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>101</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>41</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17394460</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B55"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>S-W</given-names></name><name><surname>Yi</surname><given-names>J-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Miranpuri</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Thiazolidinedione class of peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor <italic>&#x003b3;</italic> agonists prevents neuronal damage, motor dysfunction, myelin loss, neuropathic pain, and inflammation after spinal cord injury in adult rats</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Pharmacology and Experimental Therapeutics</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>320</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>1002</fpage><lpage>1012</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17167171</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><n